ible  well we're certainly going to have to  ramp up vaccination  and do many more vaccinations per day  in the first week or so we did not get  to a million  vaccinations um we need to be doing a  million vaccinations  per day to be getting to the targets  that the president-elect has  outlined so that's really going to mean  a massive increase  and again you know when you have all of  your doctors and nurses in the hospitals  taking care of sick patients who's going  to give those vaccinations  so we really have a massive manpower  problem right now  dr gander we spoke earlier this morning  with dr tom frieden who said it's so  important for people to continue wearing  those masks  and he sees that happening for the next  several months but do you  see a future in the next six months to a  year where we won't be wearing a mask or  is this sort of the new normal  for for some time  i think unfortunately this is the new  normal for some time i think  six months would be very optimistic  i don't think we're going to have  everybody vaccinated by then and i think  it's really important for people to  understand that  even once you have been vaccinated we do  not know that you can't still  get infected and transmit to other  people all we know is that it will  the vaccine will prevent you from  getting severely ill and from dying  and so even once you are vaccinated it  is really  crucial that you continue to wear a mask  in order to help contain this and you  know i can tell you i'm going to be  vaccinated later this morning myself  i will continue to wear a mask so dr  gander for the american people who  want to know the priorities of the  president-elect's administration when it  comes  to battling the coronavirus laid down  for us what do you expect to see  over the next year well i think you're  going to see a massive increase in  testing it is  really hard to contain something when  you don't know what you're even dealing  with  so it's like a big iceberg we see 